# Gate step 1118-bscs — data, not code (order 1072-b7eq).
#
# Two confinements of the same shape: a capability left open because nothing
# currently uses it. The credential helper handed a live GitHub token to any
# caller (it trusted how it was invoked); the permissive proxy port listened on
# 0.0.0.0 with allowlist-free egress, reachable from every enclave container
# whether or not anything routed there.
#
# STEP_SCRIPT is a LITERAL path on purpose (1063-nraf).
STEP_DESC="Checking the push token is GitHub-https-only and the permissive proxy port is loopback (1118-bscs)"
STEP_SCRIPT="scripts/test-credential-and-proxy-confinement.sh"
STEP_ERROR="a GitHub token can reach a non-GitHub host or travel over http, or the permissive proxy port is reachable from the enclave again (1118-bscs) — see the verdict line above"
STEP_OK="Credential and proxy confinement passed"
STEP_SECOND_REGIME="macneo 2026-09-22 darwin ok:   CONTROL: the strict port 3128 still binds for the enclave (confinement did not break the allowlisted pat"
# ORDER 2157-ginp: STEP_READS, the paths this step reads, RECORDED ONLY: never
# consulted by the class-selector skip (that is STEP_INPUTS, 2118-tnut). First
# cut: the step's own script plus every repo path it names literally.
STEP_READS="images/git/git-credential-tillandsias.sh images/proxy/squid.conf scripts/test-credential-and-proxy-confinement.sh"
# ORDER 2184-sinp: DECLARED INPUTS (2118-tnut grammar). The script reads
# exactly two repo files (the git credential helper and the proxy config) and
# runs nothing else from the tree. An ATIME TRACE of a real run agrees.
STEP_INPUTS="path:images/git/git-credential-tillandsias.sh path:images/proxy/squid.conf"
